flowchart TB
    Internet((Public Internet))
    Customer[Customer Mail Systems]
    Admin[Administrators]

    subgraph PublicEdge["Public / Edge Boundary"]
        SMTP[Postfix SMTP]
        Web[Regional Web Entry]
    end

    subgraph PrivateApp["Private Application Boundary"]
        Rspamd[Rspamd]
        MailCore[Mail Core]
        Scanners[Scanner Nodes]
        Control[Control Backend]
        IDP[ZITADEL]
        N8N[n8n]
    end

    subgraph DataBoundary["Regional Data Boundary"]
        PG[(PostgreSQL)]
        Redis[(Redis)]
        S3[(S3)]
        Secrets[OpenBao]
        Seg[SegLumberjack\nSentry-compatible observability]
    end

    subgraph AIBoundary["Regional AI Boundary"]
        AIGateway[Authenticated AI Endpoint]
        Model[Deep AI Model]
    end

    subgraph AWSOps["AWS Infrastructure Telemetry"]
        CW[CloudWatch]
    end

    subgraph ExternalOps["External / Operational Integrations"]
        ClickUp[ClickUp]
        TI[Threat Intelligence]
    end

    Internet --> SMTP
    Customer <--> SMTP
    Admin --> Web

    SMTP --> Rspamd --> MailCore
    Web --> Control
    Control --> IDP

    MailCore --> Scanners
    MailCore --> PG
    MailCore --> Redis
    MailCore --> S3
    Control --> PG
    Control --> Redis

    Secrets --> MailCore
    Secrets --> Scanners
    Secrets --> Control

    MailCore --> AIGateway --> Model
    Model --> S3

    PrivateApp -->|sanitized Sentry-compatible telemetry| Seg
    AIGateway -->|sanitized telemetry| Seg
    Model -->|sanitized telemetry| Seg

    AWS[AWS Runtime / Managed Services] --> CW

    N8N -->|minimized metadata only| ClickUp
    Scanners -->|explicit allowed fields only| TI
